// Included by `parser_golden.rs`; not a test target of its own.

/// Corpus rows this port does not reproduce, each with the reason it cannot.
///
/// Keyed by `row_id`. The replay fails if any entry here ever *passes*, so the
/// table can never quietly become a skip-list, and it fails on any mismatch that
/// is **not** listed, so it can never quietly grow. Rows are never deleted from
/// the corpus to raise the pass rate.
///
/// **333 of 7008 rows (95.2 % reproduce).** Every one is a `browser-dom`
/// parse-shape or libxml2-convention difference already accepted by
/// `ARCHITECTURE.md` §11.6 and recorded in `docs/DIVERGENCES.md`:
///
/// | rows | cause |
/// |---:|---|
/// | 70 | libxml2 gives a valueless boolean attribute (`checked`) the attribute *name* as its value; html5ever gives it `""`, which then changes every `SequenceMatcher` ratio computed over it |
/// | 68 | html5ever's synthesised `<head>` |
/// | 62 | html5ever's implied `<tbody>` |
/// | 39 | SVG/MathML camel-case local names and the `xlink:`/`xmlns` prefix split |
/// | 34 | libxml2 refuses to compile an XPath string holding a raw control character, so `find_all(..., {"title": "form\ffeed"})` raises `ValueError` in Python and simply matches here |
/// | 21 | the whitespace between `</body>` and `</html>`, which html5ever keeps inside `<body>` |
/// | 19 | html5ever cannot tell `data-x` from `data-x=""`, so it serialises the bare form with a value |
/// | 18 | the HTML5 adoption agency rebuilding `<b>`/`<i>` after the stray `</p>` in `malformed.html` |
/// | 2 | element counts on `malformed.html`'s `<html>`/`<body>`, where three of the above compound |
///
/// **Not one** of them is a `css` / `xpath` / `find_all` / `find_similar` /
/// `find_by_text` / `get_all_text` / selector-generation / fingerprint /
/// relocation *algorithm* difference: wherever the two trees agree, so do the
/// answers. All 23 end-to-end `adaptive` rows reproduce, score tables included.
